WARNING:DT_SPLIT_BINDING_PATCH: DT binding docs and includes should be a separate patch. See: Documentation/devicetree/bindings/submitting-patches.rst

Devicetree bindings should be their own patch.  This is because
bindings are logically independent from a driver implementation,
they have a different maintainer (even though they often
are applied via the same tree), and it makes for a cleaner history in the
DT only tree created with git-filter-branch.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/devicetree/bindings/submitting-patches.html#i-for-patch-submitters

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'xhci->hci_version == 0x100'
#89: FILE: drivers/usb/host/xhci.c:4084:
+	if ((xhci->quirks & XHCI_HLE_DISABLE) && (xhci->hci_version == 0x100))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

CHECK:BIT_MACRO: Prefer using the BIT macro
#104: FILE: drivers/usb/host/xhci.h:1822:
+#define XHCI_HLE_DISABLE	(1 << 27)

Defines like: 1 << <digit> could be BIT(digit).
The BIT() macro is defined via include/linux/bits.h::

  #define BIT(nr)         (1UL << (nr))

